= LEBOK – The Learning Engineering Body of Knowledge =

'''LEBOK''' is a community-maintained reference for the discipline of
'''learning engineering''': the practice of applying the learning sciences,
human-centered design, and data-informed iteration to create and improve
learning experiences. It is organized into '''[[Knowledge Areas]]''' and
maintained with editorial review, in alignment with the
[https://sagroups.ieee.org/icicle/ IEEE ICICLE] community's work toward
professional standards.

''This wiki is a working draft. Knowledge-area titles and boundaries are
pending confirmation by the working group — pages marked '''Draft''' are
starting points for community revision, not settled positions.''

== Knowledge Areas ==

The full index, including status, is at '''[[Knowledge Areas]]'''.
Drafted so far:

* [[KA5: Instructional Strategy Design]]
* [[KA6: Learning Experience Design]]
* [[KA10: Evaluation and Continuous Improvement]]
* [[KA11: Research Methods]]

== How this wiki works ==

Anyone can propose an edit — create an account and click ''Edit'' on any
page. Proposed changes go into a moderation queue and are reviewed by
editors before they publish, so the version you are reading has always
passed editorial review. See '''[[LEBOK:Contributing]]''' for how to make
a change, citation expectations, and how trusted contributors gain direct
edit rights.

== The wider ecosystem ==

LEBOK is one part of the Learning Engineering Commons:

* [https://lecommons.org The Learning Engineering Commons] — the hub: people, organizations, and resources of the field
* [https://capabilitymatters.org LENS @ JHU] — evidence and editorial analysis, including the [https://capabilitymatters.org/graph capability graph] and [https://capabilitymatters.org/resources resource library]
* [https://sagroups.ieee.org/icicle/ IEEE ICICLE] — the industry consortium for learning engineering standards
* [https://github.com/wrgr/lebok LEBOK on GitHub] — backups (XML dumps) and tooling for this wiki

